course: dictionary
lesson: 15729
title: Transform: change completely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To transform something is to change it so much that it looks or works in a new way. Often the change makes it better. «The shed was transformed with bright paint, a rug and a big window.» The shed did not just get a new coat of paint. It became a new kind of place.
explain: Look for the clue words around transform. Words like «into», «from» and «became» show that something has changed shape or form. «A caterpillar transforms into a butterfly.» The caterpillar does not just grow bigger. It turns into something different.
explain: Transform is also used in maths and science. In maths, a shape can be moved, flipped, turned or enlarged, and each of these is a transformation. In science, energy is transformed when it changes from one type into another, such as a battery's energy becoming light.
fact: To transform something means to change it completely, often making it better.
fact: To transform is to change from one form or shape into another, as a tadpole transforms into a frog.
fact: In maths, a transformation moves or changes a shape by a translation, reflection, rotation or enlargement.
fact: In science, «The torch transforms the energy in its battery into light.»
fact: In stories, a magic wand can transform a frog into a prince.
exercise: «The shed was transformed into a cosy reading den.» What does transformed mean here? | Painted one colour only | Moved a little to the left | *Changed completely, often for the better | Knocked down and left empty
exercise: «A tadpole transforms into a frog.» What happens to the tadpole? | It swims away to find food | It sleeps all winter | *It changes into a frog | It grows a longer tail
exercise: «The torch transforms the energy in its battery into light.» What is the energy turned into? | Sound | Heat only | Water | *Light
test: In maths, which of these is NOT a way to transform a shape? | Enlargement | *Colouring it in | Reflection | Rotation
test: «With one wave of her wand, the fairy transformed the frog into a prince.» What did the fairy do? | Kissed the frog | Put the frog in a pond | Made the frog hop away | *Changed the frog into a prince
exam: «The new playground transformed our school.» What does this mean? | Broke the school windows | *Changed our school completely, making it better | Painted one wall only | Moved the school to a new street
